cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark in research, cite it with the release_id and the
  commit, not the repository alone. A release is a pinned set of problems and
  environment; the repository moves.
title: "mathdb-lean problems"
abstract: >-
  Mathematical problems formalized as frozen Lean 4 propositions, one folder per
  problem, with the pinned Lean project they compile against and the record of
  what was released. The erdos-reviewed release holds 704 problems and 1106 proof
  obligations derived from the Erdos problems collection. Every obligation
  elaborates, reaches only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound, matches its
  declared interface, and survived a tactic suite; none has been read by a person.
type: dataset
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mathdb-lean/problems"
authors:
  # Add individual authors here. The copyright headers throughout this
  # repository name the collective, so that is what is cited until they do.
  - name: "The mathdb-lean Authors"
version: "erdos-reviewed"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - formal mathematics
  - theorem proving
  - benchmark
  - erdos problems
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Formal Conjectures"
    abstract: >-
      The upstream corpus these problems and the vendored support libraries are
      derived from, at revision e04cc601840dd7a37f89b821a67f3a9e3c38d9c3.
    repository-code: "https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures"
    license: Apache-2.0
    authors:
      - name: "Google DeepMind and the Formal Conjectures Authors"
